WEBVTT

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:02.770
I heard they won the New Artist Award.

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.100
Congratulations.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.560
<i>I wanted to tell them myself.</i>

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.040
Thank you. They were all so happy.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.190
Naturally they were happy 
about winning the award,

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:12.860
but also,

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.510
<i>to be challenging reigning champions 
TRIGGER at the end of the year.</i>

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.290
Yeah, I'm looking forward to it, too.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:20.370
What's so funny?

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:27.450
You're the one who anonymously 
recommended IDOLiSH7 for <i>Music Festa</i>.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.460
<i>I don't know what you're talking about.</i>

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.210
Oh, right.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.180
There's a soba deliveryman near our 
office who looks just like you.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:35.970
<i>Really?</i>

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.970
Next time you're over, I'll—

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.550
Oh, there won't be a next time.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.480
After all, TRIGGER and 
IDOLiSH7 are rivals now.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.480
You're right.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.470
Once they lose to us, 
I'm sure you'll hate us.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.190
<i>IDOLiSH7 won't lose.</i>

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.310
Neither will we.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.370
Talk to you later.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.110
The next time we meet will 
be at <i>Black or White</i>.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:55.810
Yes.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:56.710
<i>Goodnight.</i>

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.780
Who was that?

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.150
Oh, um... TRIGGER's Yaotome-san.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.120
He congratulated us on  
the New Artist Award.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.960
He bothered to call?

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.790
What a conscientious person.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.000
Yeah...

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.470
So the boys won the JIMA New Artist Award.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:16.430
It's inspiring, isn't it?

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.680
Yes. I feel like I'm dreaming.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.660
To be honest, I used to play music, too.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.850
Really?

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:29.480
Yes, so it feels like they 
made my dream come true.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:34.190
I hope they become
 internationally famous.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.040
You don't think I'm being 
too ambitious, do you?

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:37.940
Not at all.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:41.210
IDOLiSH7's potential is limitless.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.910
Yes, this is Takanashi.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.650
Huh? Uh, sorry?

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.000
Pardon?!

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:56.450
IDOLiSH7 will sing happily for you.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.130
Sure. See you.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:01.050
Nagi-san, what did he say?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:04.770
Douglas Rootbank will be coming to 
Japan for his Christmas performance.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.130
He wants us to open for him.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.770
Douglas Rootbank?

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:15.400
Popular American pop-rock 
singer Douglas Rootbank?!

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.360
What?!

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:17.930
Yes.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:21.240
Douglas Rootbank...

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.130
The president and Osaka-san 
were rather excited yesterday.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:25.950
Yeah.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.360
Since So-chan's so smart, he 
likes songs in English, too.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.750
I don't think those are related.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.630
<b>Collect all 5
 Original Mascot
 Limited Special Charm</b>

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.880
You don't want that bonus item?

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.630
Nah.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:39.700
It'd be a waste to throw 
it away, so I'll take it.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.890
I'm just trying to recycle.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.350
When does the meeting start?

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.280
It should be starting soon.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.880
Yes, who is—

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.250
<b>Donburi</b>

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.150
IDOLiSH—

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:53.610
Why'd you close it?

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.920
There was some kind of weirdo.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.650
What?

00:02:55.650 --> 00:03:00.050
As a child, I was taught not to 
answer the door for strange people.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.990
I'll answer it.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:07.660
IDOLiSH7, my name—

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.750
You were right.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:09.330
See?

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.920
He looked like a namahage ogre.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.360
Is he a stalker?

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:19.050
Maybe he's the guy Manager mentioned 
who's here to install the screen.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.220
Yeah.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.980
Nice to meet you.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.890
My name is—

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:26.890
H-Hey! Don't hug me!

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.130
Oh, sorry. My name is—

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.840
Look, Mister, we're underage.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:34.770
We need an adult to help us 
understand difficult concepts.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:37.650
Hello.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.280
Hello.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.650
My name—

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.650
This way, please.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.780
Oh. My name is—

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:47.530
I guess they send foreign workers 
to install foreign-made screens.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:52.020
It's not here. The screen's not here yet.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:52.810
Okay?

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:53.790
Not here?

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.840
He understood me.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.630
Iorin, I can speak English.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.260
Then ask if he needs a stepladder.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.390
Lad... der...

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.020
Up and down.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.790
Y-Yeah?

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.270
He needs one!

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.690
Lad... der?

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.160
Feet here, okay?

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:17.360
Foot goes here.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.120
Okay, okay.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.040
Could you have him remove 
the light cover while he's at it?

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.400
It's dirty.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.410
Sorry I'm la—

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.140
Welcome back.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.870
What's up, Rikkun?

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:36.660
Wh-Why is Douglas Rootbank 
replacing our light cover?!

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.000
My name is—

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.370
Douglas?

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.260
Rootbank?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.050
I'm terribly sorry about what happened!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.810
Oh, no problem.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:55.510
We will work diligently to ensure 
nothing like this ever happens again!

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:58.400
Oh, Sogo. I can't translate all of that.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:04.930
Tell him I'd be happy to give him my pinky 
finger to compensate for this offense!

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.450
No, keep your finger.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:11.200
I had no idea Douglas-san 
was coming to the office.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.380
I'm overjoyed!

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:12.740
Huh?

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.030
So am I!

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:14.660
What?

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.820
I just wanted to surprise you.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:21.170
Apparently he wanted to surprise us.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.650
These guys are huge fans.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.640
You should get his autograph.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:27.010
What? I can't...

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.060
...ask for his...

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.140
...autograph...

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.480
What? No, I couldn't...

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.640
Sir, you can't be nervous, too.

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.140
Here you go.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.350
Thank you.

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:42.840
Even if my entire room goes up in flames, 
tell him I swear to protect this.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:46.700
Oh. Sogo, your expressions are too much.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:50.810
You didn't even get mad at me when
 I made you get a hole in your stomach,

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.610
but this old dude—

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.940
Don't call him an old dude.

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:57.410
But you got all pissed that I made 
Douglas replace our light cover.

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.750
I was pissed off, too.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.200
I nearly committed harakiri 
to make up for it.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.960
Aren't you more important that him?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.840
Douglas is more important.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.090
Whoa...

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:15.780
"I saw that very seven in a video 
and I knew they would be stars,

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.340
because they rocked my heart.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:23.080
I thought I should meet them.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.280
I'm happy to celebrate 
Christmas with you guys.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.610
Let's spend a super sizzling night."

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.200
...Is what he said.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:34.020
We have a great musician here in our office.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:36.290
Why don't you ask him something?

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:38.680
A question, huh?

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:39.960
Excuse me...

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.900
We have a big performance coming up.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.110
We'll be competing against our rivals there.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.680
"We have a big performance coming up.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.400
Is there some secret to beating them?

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:50.120
We'll be competing against our rivals there.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:53.350
If I knew I'd be talking to Douglas, 
I would've studied English harder.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.350
Is there some secret to beating them?"

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.890
"It's God that decides who wins.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:02.290
But what we need to better ourselves is love."

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.110
Love...

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:14.490
"You hear songs through your ears, but when 
you hear songs that have love in them,

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.420
your heart starts to rumble first, 
and then your body starts to dance.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:21.000
Zero's songs were just like that."

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.210
Zero?!

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.080
Douglas-san, you know Zero?!

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.780
Yes, I love Zero.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.210
We love Zero.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.750
"I've met Zero only once.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:39.810
Hearing his song right before me was 
a valuable experience for me in life."

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:41.830
Miracle.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.260
"I felt like I was struck 
by something magical."

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.480
Zero's amazing!

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:54.710
"Zero certainly knew what love is, 
and what it means to be loved."

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:03.850
Douglas Rootbank Exclusive Interview!

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:03.850
I can't believe they're 
opening for Douglas Rootbank.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.820
Lucky them. I'm a huge fan.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.380
If my schedule were open, I'd go.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:13.210
We opened for an English diva.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.390
How can you be so calm?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:19.560
The <i>Black or White</i> vote 
is open to the public.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:22.060
The more people talk about them, 
the more votes they'll take—

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:24.060
Then we'll take them back.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.010
Well, no matter how much
 this gets people talking,

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:30.320
it just means they're finally 
on equal footing with us.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.220
A tense race isn't so bad.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:37.410
Let's show our strong challengers 
a champion's dignity.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:42.500
We'll settle the score at <i>Black or White</i>.

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.980
The year's nearly over.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:51.800
Will the start of the approaching 
new year be met magnificently

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.300
by last year's champions 
or their challengers?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.320
Yours could be the deciding vote.

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:04.810
The <i>Black or White Music Fantasia</i> starts now.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:15.350
Hey.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:16.990
Hello.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.770
I'm going to make your brother and Ryu win.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:20.910
No hard feelings.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.830
Well, I'll make my friends win.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:26.710
I'll stand in the center and 
pull them along with me!

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:31.300
You've got guts.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.500
Good luck, Nanase.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.480
You too, Yaotome-san.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:35.570
Riku.

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.670
Tenn-nii.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:39.050
I wasn't expecting to meet you on this stage.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:41.860
I won't hold back.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.430
Good luck tonight, IDOLiSH7.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.890
You, too!

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.660
It's nearly time.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:52.100
Are you nervous?

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:52.860
A little.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.240
This side of you is cute.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.340
Shut up.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:57.900
I'm glad.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:02.240
We get to challenge them 
head on with our own song.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.450
Yeah.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:08.260
Let's not embarrass ourselves in 
front of them or the audience.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:15.460
Win or lose, let's make this a 
supremely euphoric performance.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.830
We'll win.

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:18.980
Yeah.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:20.260
Hey.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.220
Should we high five or something?

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.210
What?

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.830
This is why I can't stand kids.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:29.450
Sorry. I'll never mention it again.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:30.100
Sheesh.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:33.610
Let's go, TRIGGER!

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:38.820
Yeah!

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:41.280
You're not very honest.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.360
Shut it!

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:49.050
Next up is last year's winners of 
the male idol category, TRIGGER!

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.990
Listen to that crowd.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:53.290
Thank you.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:56.300
We made it this far thanks to our fans.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.400
I heard you're performing a new song tonight.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.470
It's a song only we can sing.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.890
Do you have a message for 
your challengers, IDOLiSH7?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.140
They're a worthy opponent.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:10.760
This is TRIGGER, performing "Leopard Eyes."

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:28.040
Taste you Taste you…

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.290
Taste me Taste me…

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:36.420
Melty love Melty kiss…

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:49.540
The moonlight casts a spell on the city

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:53.670
Wo Wow it is an Illusion

00:11:55.730 --> 00:12:04.490
The Highway slips between the buildings

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:08.450
Wo Wow the wind blows along it

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:17.000
There's no point in searching for an escape

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:12.000
Whoa...

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:15.070
This song is TRIGGER on full blast.

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:17.000
I'm sure their fans are enjoying it.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:19.560
TRIGGER's world view is totally complete.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:24.800
I want to destroy that innocence

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:21.250
Whoa, those moves.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:23.130
It's amazing they can pull them off.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.800
It's great!

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.710
Since that day we watched TRIGGER's concert

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:30.880
and started singing together, 
we finally made it this far.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:34.010
Let's give everything we've got 
and stand side by side with them!

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:36.040
We'll surpass them.

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:40.360
Anyway, the arena is huge.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.110
And so is the audience.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.000
It's our first time performing on this scale.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.760
Tama, this year-end show has the 
highest ratings of any in Japan.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.280
Your sister's probably watching.

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:52.090
Yeah.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:57.000
Hey, why did we become idols?

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:00.980
Didn't you do it to find your sister?

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:03.550
Yeah, but that's not what I meant.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:08.220
The guys on stage say thank you all the time.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:12.960
I thought they were just saying 
it because it felt good.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.420
But I was wrong.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:15.730
You're right.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.980
It really does come welling 
up from your heart.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:22.280
It feels strange to make others happy 
by just doing what you want.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.070
It makes you want to make 
them even happier next time.

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:27.430
And the next, and the next.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.270
More and more and more.

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:30.740
The feeling bubbles over.

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:33.250
It's like Douglas said.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.320
It's what Zero knew.

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:40.710
We have to win!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:44.870
Good luck.

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.720
Do your best, guys.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.720
I'll be rooting for you.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.490
Manager...

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:55.510
You idiot, it's too soon to cry.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:58.650
We're about to show you 
something even better.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.570
Yes, smile.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.610
I promise we'll win tonight.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:06.500
It only makes up for a fraction 
of all the worry we've caused.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:07.700
But we'll do it.

